# gl2-probe's identity, reserved before there is anything to build.
#
# **Why this exists ahead of the code.** Two things here are cheap now and expensive later, and
# both were learned the hard way on the apps beside this one:
#
#   - **A derived identifier collides.** Without `EXPLICIT_TITLE_ID` the id is derived from the
#     app's name, and `gl2-cube` records that its derived id would have been `PROG00001` - which
#     `gl1-probe` also derived. Two apps with one id only show up the first time both are
#     installed, which is a long way from here.
#   - **The letter field takes no digits.** `gl2-cube` was `GL2C00001` and the console's
#     installer refused it outright: measured on `gl1-probe`'s `GL1P00001`, whose deploy staged
#     cleanly and was then never indexed (`20 Invalid TitleId`,
#     `AppPromote Error ... 0x80bd000a`). `app.mk` checks the shape now, but the name still has
#     to be chosen with it in mind.
#
# So `GLTP00001` - GL Two Probe, matching `GLTC00001` for GL Two Cube. Four letters, five digits,
# no digit among the letters.
#
# `FORMATS=eboot title` since 2026-09-22. It was `check-only` for as long as there was no console
# back end for a GL 2.0 program: a payload would have reported every drawing check as failed for
# one reason upstream of all of them, and measured nothing that was not already written down.
# There is a back end now, so the same checks measure the console. See README.md.
EXPLICIT_TITLE_ID=1
TITLE_ID=GLTP00001
TITLE_NAME="GL2 Probe"
APP_SUBTITLE="OpenGL 2.0 conformance probe"
TITLE_CATEGORY=big-app
TITLE_VERSION=01.00
FORMATS=eboot title
